<!-- First-Timer FAQ -->
<section class="faq-section section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow">Plain Answers for First-Timers</span>
    <h2>Before You Book: What Couples Ask Most</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-accordion-wrapper">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Do we have to be in "the lifestyle" to visit Desire?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>No. Many guests are simply everyday couples looking to escape routine, enjoy a beautiful tropical beach, and experience clothing-optional freedom without judgment. You will see all ages, body types, and backgrounds. The primary rule is mutual respect.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What does clothing-optional actually mean in practice?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>It means clothes are strictly optional in the pool and beach areas during daytime hours. You may wear swimwear, casual linen cover-ups, or nothing at all. For indoor evening dining, plan for elegant resort-chic attire (such as collared shirts and tailored pants or shorts for men; sundresses, jumpsuits, or evening resort wear for women).</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Are we pressured to interact with other couples?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Not at all. Your boundaries are absolute. If you want a private getaway focused entirely on each other, that is completely respected. If you wish to socialize at the swim-up bar, conversations flow naturally and easily.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What are the photography rules?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Discretion and consent come first. Our concierge advice is to treat photography as strictly private and keep phones tucked away in public social areas, pools, and night venues so everyone can relax completely. Always follow the resort&rsquo;s official house rules regarding device use.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Which resort should we choose for our first stay?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Couples looking for a boutique, romantic, and relaxed setting generally prefer <strong>Desire Pearl</strong>. Couples seeking high daytime energy, pool activities, and vibrant late-night dancing tend to love <strong>Desire Riviera Maya</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

